# Real-Time Examples

GPS Navigation
Navigation systems need to find suitable paths between locations. A* can consider the distance already travelled and the estimated distance to the destination.

Robot Navigation
A warehouse robot may need to travel from its starting position to a particular shelf while avoiding obstacles. A* can identify an efficient path.

Video Games
In games, characters need to move from one location to another while avoiding walls and obstacles. A* is commonly used for pathfinding.

Autonomous Systems
Autonomous machines need to make decisions about movement and routes. Heuristic search can help them find suitable paths efficiently.
